  <title xml:lang="EN">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Youth Online Navigation &#x2013; AI as Game Changer</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2" xml:lang="EN">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Social media platforms have emerged as vital spaces for democratic debate and dialogue specially for young generations. 
However, the rise of hate speech and slurs is increasingly undermining these discussions. At the same time, artificial 
intelligence (AI) is transforming every sector, including the field of human rights. With its current capabilities, AI can be 
developed to effectively moderate online spaces and help restore a safe space for this public discourse. It&apos;s time to harness 
this potential.
The overall goal of the project is to use AI to develop a highly innovative tool serving the promotion of inclusive online 
spaces with less hate speech across the MENA region through more innovative and effective moderation of social media.
Expected Outcomes
&#x2022; Safer online spaces where media and CSOs can engage their audiences without fear of harassment or 
manipulation.
&#x2022; Strengthened capacity for participating partners within the DAPP consortia to manage digital interactions 
effectively.
&#x2022; Engaging social media comment sections, enabling constructive dialogue instead of silencing audiences.</narrative>
  </description>
